From: xleng <991350086@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:54:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(subprocess): name the /proc process-tree platform
 set

createProcessInspector and the process-group liveness rule in spawn.ts each
compared the target platform against the 'linux' literal, so the set of
platforms that serve the Linux-style /proc process tree lived in two places and
was named by an operating system rather than by the requirement.

Android is Linux-family: bionic serves /proc/<pid>/stat and /proc/<pid>/task in
the layout both readers parse, and os.platform() reports 'android'. The literal
therefore excluded a platform whose readers work unchanged, and terminal
inspection threw at plugin load on that platform.

Export hasProcProcessTree(platform) from process-inspector.ts and call it from
both readers. createProcessInspector keeps its fail-loud throw for every other
platform.
